MIT was chosen after checking it against everything this repository redistributes. It is compatible
with all of it:

- the bundled runtime is Apache-2.0 with the LLVM exception, Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD-2-Clause,
  BSD-3-Clause and CC0;
- `@wasm-idle/llvm-core` is MIT and Apache-2.0 with the LLVM exception.

Nothing here is copyleft, so nothing here restricts what you can do with the programs you compile.

This covers the code written for this repository: the demo page with its worker and server, and the
package in packages/clang-wasm.

It does not cover the third-party binaries that ship alongside it, which keep their own licenses.
Those are listed, each with what it is and where it came from, in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.
